Z||000000||camon||12-01-2001||03:50 AM||||Well the weekend has arrived and I plan on fixing my rear brake rattle (replacing rear pads) and i'm also gonna throw on a new fuel filter I purcashed a while back, while the rear end is up in the air.<P>This will also be a good time to take measurements that I was asked to take of the Catalytic Coverter.<BR>I'm gonna be replacing the CAT soon with a Rodney Dickman's CAT kit and I emailed him to findout if his kit will work with the exhualst system on my car (it was replaced by the orginal owner a few years ago and i'm not sure if the CAT he offers will bolt right up....not sure what type of exhualst system the original owner put on here ). Well Rodney told me to take measurements and get the ID.<P>Does anyone know what he needs measured ( pipe diameter measurements and the cat measurements from weld bead to weld bead) or what exactly???? <P>I'm posting this question here because I will probably get a quicker response from this board them I would if I emailed him directly! <P>And also where is this "ID"????<P>Thanks<P>------------------<BR>   Keith<BR>1987 Fiero GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||tesmith66||12-01-2001||07:13 AM||||ID stands for inside diameter.<BR>(OD stands for outside diameter)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>All he would need is the length between welds and the ID of the converter pipe. If it appears to have been slipped over the exhaust pipe and welded, just measure the od of the exhaust pipe.<P>------------------<BR>Timothy E. Smith<BR>1986 SE V6<BR>1984 Coupe||||reg||1
